{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f4ed024ea25852b4","name":"LE-Series Repair Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-f4ed024ea25852b4","title":"LE-Series Repair Droid","revision":19965,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:56:39Z","sha256":"f96e751284a45ecf5c274c18998996fffd7c48025109b7d8352295ed0d050c82","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19965","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=LE-Series%20Repair%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f4ed024ea25852b4","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The concept behind Cybot Galactica's LE-Series Repair Droid is simple enough: combine the repair functions of an Astromech Droid with the chassis and personality matrix of an Administrative Droid. With the hopes of appealing to a market of independent traders and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"}," captains, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybot Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybot_Galactica","referenceId":"reference:8d89ff519236e3e2"}," advertised the LE-Series Droid as having extensive functionality concentrated into one Droid, and the corporation asked a high price for them.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The main drawback is the bipedal, humanoid chassis. Although it helps the Droid to more easily interact with spaceport officials and docking crews, the design hampers its primary function as a Repair Droid. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybot Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybot_Galactica","referenceId":"reference:8d89ff519236e3e2"}," insists that the LE-Series can use the same tools as its owner and emphasizes that the administration skills programming allows it to handle the day-to-day duties that ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," captains want to avoid. However, the company's efforts fall on deaf ears.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["LE-Series Droids are found on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," and in port offices, acting as administrative assistants, though their technical skills do occasionally come into play to help repair office equipment.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["LE-Series Repair Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["LE-Series Repair Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["2nd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/2nd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +0; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 1 Unassigned; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Translator Unit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Translator_Unit","referenceId":"reference:0bcd4b383b11cac0"}," (DC 15)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"